# Off-Target · CITATION.cff
# How to cite this repository. GitHub reads this file and shows "Cite this repository".
# The author list mirrors the article's byline, AI co-author included, because the
# record should say who did the work. What Flame is: docs/READING-THE-RECORD.md. To cite the work under review, use the authors'
# own citation, which is the first reference below and is given in full in NOTICE.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Off-Target: a design change review of an AI-authored weight edit"
abstract: >-
  A review of the weight edit published in "Sparks of Weight-Space Programming" (Takehi, Teoh,
  Zhang and Khattab, November 2026), done the way a design change to a regulated product is
  reviewed: a bit-level diff, provenance checks against the authors' logs, three pre-registered
  reruns, and a one-command check that recomputes every claimed number from the result files.
authors:
  - family-names: Johnson
    given-names: Angela N.
    affiliation: The Real Cat Labs
  - name: "Flame, AI co-author (The Real Cat Labs)"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Angiebio/off-target-demo"
url: "https://github.com/Angiebio/off-target-demo"
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - weight editing
  - change control
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: blog
    title: "Sparks of Weight-Space Programming: LLMs can natively read & write neural network weights"
    authors:
      - family-names: Takehi
        given-names: Rikiya
      - family-names: Teoh
        given-names: Jayden
      - family-names: Zhang
        given-names: Alex
      - family-names: Khattab
        given-names: Omar
    url: "https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/"
    year: 2026
    month: 11
    notes: "The work under review. Logs at github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs, commit 4d09ba6, CC BY 4.0."
  - type: article
    title: "What really happens when a dev vibes with the code? An empirical study on LLM behavioral divergence in response to expressive code comments"
    authors:
      - family-names: Johnson
        given-names: Angela N.
    journal: "Frontiers in Artificial Intelligence"
    volume: 9
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.3389/frai.2026.1784973"
    notes: "A pilot study by this repository's first author, cited in docs/DESIGN.md for the choice to write comments as briefings."
